52
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:31,420
Freehold isn't automatically
the better investment,

53
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:33,940
and leasehold isn't
automatically the worst one.

54
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:38,080
A leasehold flat with 900 years
remaining and a low ground rent behaves

55
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:42,400
very differently to one with 60 years
left and an escalating rent clause.

56
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,980
I wouldn't rule out leasehold
completely, but I'd want a strong gross

57
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:49,630
yield going in, so that the
service charge and the ground rent

58
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:52,600
don't leave me with a low net
yield once they're accounted for.

59
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:57,570
What matters is understanding the
specific lease terms or the specific

60
